## Production and Material Optimization

Manufacturing operations were organized through defined work centers, production routings, and Gantt-based scheduling.

A Cutting Stock optimization model was applied to reduce material waste, obtaining 12 bases per aluminum sheet and an estimated waste cost of €3.13 per lamp.

The selected production lot of 231 units supported the planned annual production of 6,930 lamps.

## Excel vs. SAP Cost Comparison

One of the main outcomes was the comparison between standard production costs calculated manually in Excel and those obtained through SAP.

The analysis covered individual semi-finished products, the finished lamp, and cumulative cost deviations.

The comparison showed small differences between the two calculation methods, supporting the consistency of the engineering cost model and its implementation in SAP.

## Interpretation

The results demonstrate how engineering calculations can be translated into an integrated manufacturing planning environment.

Production scheduling, material requirements, lot-sizing decisions, and cost calculations provided a quantitative foundation for SAP PP/MM configuration.

The comparison between Excel and SAP also provided a means of validating the manufacturing cost structure and identifying deviations between the two approaches.

**Final Outcome:** The project established a complete manufacturing planning model for the PHOS Smart Lamp, connecting product engineering, production optimization, material management, and SAP-based cost analysis.
